This repository contains the source code and assets of the game "Autocrat"
(formerly "Seraph Breaker"). The source is published so that people can read
it, play the game, and contribute to it through pull requests. It is NOT open
source. Except for the permissions written below, all rights are reserved by
the copyright holder ("the Owner").

1. DEFINITIONS

"The Software" means everything in this repository and in the published game:
source code, data tables, 3D models and the code that builds them, designs and
documents (including the pages under docs/), text, story, characters, names
(including "Autocrat" and "Seraph Breaker"), user interface, sounds, music
setups, images and screenshots.

2. WHAT YOU MAY DO

a) Read and study the source code in this repository.
b) Run the Software on your own device to play it or to test it, for your own
   personal, non-commercial use.
c) Fork this repository on GitHub, and make changes in that fork, solely to
   prepare and submit contributions back to this repository through pull
   requests.
d) Make and share videos, streams and screenshots of yourself playing the
   published game, including monetized ones, as long as you do not share the
   game files themselves.

3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

Without the Owner's prior written permission you may not:

a) copy, distribute, publish, host, mirror, sell, rent or sublicense the
   Software or any part of it, whether modified or not;
b) use the Software or any part of it for any commercial purpose, including
   advertising, in-app purchases, donations tied to a copy of the game, game
   portals or app stores;
c) create or publish a derivative work, including a renamed, reskinned,
   translated or otherwise modified version of the game, or another game that
   reuses its code, data, models, designs, story or characters;
d) use the names "Autocrat" or "Seraph Breaker", the characters, the story or
   the art of the Software to identify any other product;
e) use the Software to train or fine-tune machine learning models, or to build
   datasets for that purpose;
f) remove or change this license or any copyright notice.

Forks that exist only to submit pull requests must not be published or played
by others outside GitHub's own fork view.

